MBSA integration
MBSA derives the MXFP6 index scorers' DeepGEMM code from
https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM, via the maxwell-model/DeepGEMM fork
(https://github.com/maxwell-model/DeepGEMM):

  python/mbsa/mxfp6/csrc/sm100_utils.cuh
    Definitions from deep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/{common,ptx,mma}/ in
    maxwell-model/DeepGEMM, reduced to what the scorers use.
  python/mbsa/mxfp6/csrc/paged_mqa_logits_scheduler.cuh
    deep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/scheduler/paged_mqa_logits.cuh from
    deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM, reformatted.
  python/mbsa/mxfp6/csrc/sm100_fp6_paged_mqa_logits.cuh
    Derived from deep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/impls/
    sm100_fp4_paged_mqa_logits.cuh in deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM.
  python/mbsa/mxfp6/csrc/fp6_dg_ext.cu
    Derived from the public host launcher in csrc/jit_kernels/impls/
    smxx_fp8_fp4_paged_mqa_logits.hpp in deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM.
    MBSA adds the Torch extension entry point, tensor-map descriptor cache,
    MXFP6 operands, validation and
    the page max/sum score interface.

DeepSeek's copyright and MIT license identifiers are retained in each file
header. Maxwell Team's modifications are released under the same MIT license.
PROVENANCE.md and UPSTREAM.json record upstream paths, Git blobs and hashes.
No DeepGEMM or CUTLASS header tree is vendored.
